{"name":"Rockmelon Rind","hex":"#d3e0b1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rockmelon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A type of melon, Cucumis melo var. reticulatus, with sweet orange flesh and a rough skin resembling netting."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rockmelon"},{"term":"rind","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Tree bark.","A hard, tough outer layer, particularly on food such as fruit, cheese, etc."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To remove the rind from."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rind"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cantaloupe","blocks":[{"text":"The cantaloupe is a type of true melon with sweet, aromatic, and usually orange flesh. Originally, cantaloup referred to the true cantaloupe or European cantaloupe with non- to slightly netted and often ribbed rind. Today, it also refers to the muskmelon with strongly netted rind, which is called cantaloupe in North America, rockmelon in Australia and New Zealand, and spanspek in Southern Africa. Cantaloupes range in mass from 0.5 to 5 kilograms."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Meloen_vrucht_met_bloem.jpg/330px-Meloen_vrucht_met_bloem.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cantaloupe"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Cucumis_melo_var._reticulatus_%28photo_by_Scott_Bauer%29.jpg/500px-Cucumis_melo_var._reticulatus_%28photo_by_Scott_Bauer%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Cucumis_melo_var._reticulatus_%28photo_by_Scott_Bauer%29.jpg/1280px-Cucumis_melo_var._reticulatus_%28photo_by_Scott_Bauer%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Cucumis_melo_var._reticulatus_%28photo_by_Scott